Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?bd-4d6172:=20per-node=20reintegration=20gate-ti?=
 =?UTF-8?q?meout=20override=20(winmini=3D4800s)=20=E2=80=94=20interim=20ba?=
 =?UTF-8?q?nd-aid=20for=20slow-node=20gate=20timeouts?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The merge-queue reintegration gate on winmini (a slow mini-PC) times out at the
default 2400s while cold-compiling cargo test-small, so its gate never completes
(node-wide reint rejections + dead letters + stale temp checkouts/locks).

Fix (ms-dev-ctrl-confirmed option (a) — PER-NODE, not a global bump): add a
per-NODE gate-timeout override so a slow node gets a longer gate WITHOUT raising
the global ceiling. A global bump would blunt the ~60min lands-gap wedge
detection (a 60min gate becomes ambiguous with a stale-lock wedge), so the
per-node value is set clearly ABOVE 60min.

- caco-config model.rs: NodeEntry.reintegration_gate_timeout_secs: Option<u64>.
- caco-cli lib.rs (the CACO_REINTEGRATION_GATE_TIMEOUT_SECS export): resolve the
  per-node override FIRST, then the project agent_defaults value, then the
  compiled 2400s default (env left unset).
- .cacophony/config.yaml: winmini reintegration_gate_timeout_secs: 4800 (80min,
  clearly above the ~60min wedge-detection mark per the ms-dev ctrl's tweak).
- caco-config validate.rs: reject a 0 per-node value (mirrors the project
  agent_defaults validation) + 2 tests (reject-zero, accept-positive).

Contained interim band-aid; the DURABLE fix is the ms-dev ctrl's sccache
warm-cache pairing (separate follow-up, ms-dev-ctrl-owned). This per-node band-aid
does not preclude sccache (sccache may later obviate it).

EDIT-HERE-LAND-THERE handoff: implemented on Apple-only ms-mac (cannot run the
heavy reintegration gate here per the placement policy). BLIND-CODED — NOT
compile-checked locally. Before landing, an ms-dev gated dev must: cargo check
--workspace --tests + cargo clippy --workspace + cargo test-small (esp. the 2 new
caco-config validate tests + that the caco-cli export compiles), and regenerate
the config-schema docs (just docs-build / just docs-check, since a new NodeEntry
field was added). NOT pushed by me, per ctrl — the ms-dev ctrl assigns the lander.
